      "review": {
        "finding": "Accept the Meshy-normal variant. At identical geometry, material, lighting, and cameras it keeps coherent relief on the roof ribs, fascia, columns, foliage, and planters. Reject the dense-donor normal for runtime because it creates dark roof-panel halos and harsher patching on ribs and columns.",
        "knownLimitations": [
          "The source retains fused and crumpled foliage in several garlands and planters.",
          "The translucent roof panels retain visible surface-texture variation and are not pristine architectural glass.",
          "The projection audit measures normalized surface proximity and approximate cage-ray coverage; it does not prove a clean tangent-space texture bake.",
          "The dense-donor bake is retained for audit evidence, but its visible artifacts make it unsuitable for the runtime candidate."
        ]
      }
    }
